interfaces.notes:
Learned weights (38-40) read journal 'placebo.json' gate_z95 from journal.STATE and call walk_forward_weights; otherwise the priors. Broker at line 45: PaperBroker(starting_cash, slippage_bps, commission_per_share). The loop, lines 50-75:
- fill the previous pending at {**close, **open} of bar d, with cooldown = dates[i + stop_cooldown_days] (bar-indexed, line 57);
- mark at the close (62);
- maybe_reset_peak(prev_regime) AFTER the mark (65); live does it BEFORE the mark (cycle.py:245 vs 247);
- build_targets;
- changed = regime or dd_state change;
- set dd_state; new pending when on_cycle ((i+phase) % every == 0), changed, or flat; otherwise exits-only for stops.
Result (77-93): summary() on strategy, SPY-labelled benchmark (key 'benchmark_spy') and equal-weight, plus n_trades, final_weights, final_positions, _equity (Series), _fills.

ProcessPoolExecutor is imported LOCALLY (141), so tests cannot patch it at module level. Phases come from base_every = cfg rebalance_every_days (147). Each variant is paired with the variant literally named 'base' at phase k % base_every (152-156). Summary rows hold the medians, wins_vs_base and d_sharpe_med, then the two benchmark rows. DSR (167-175):
- n_prev = sum(len(rows)) over trials.jsonl records that have 'rows';
- srs = per-variant median sharpe / sqrt(252);
- rf_d uses 1/252;
- dsr(base phase-0 daily - rf_d, n_prev + len(srs), srs.std());
- the whole block sits in a broad except that prints 'DSR unavailable'.
